WEBVTT

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:03.770
The chairman of the FSC Group is my father.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:06.360
You finally told us about yourself.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:10.440
We just have to become popular enough 
that we're beyond your dad's reach.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.650
I feel like So-chan and I are a real duo now.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.670
The Japan Idol Music Awards' 
new artist award.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:21.000
If you win, I'll tell Riku 
what he wants to know.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.540
I'm off to the meeting.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.160
Sure. See you later.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.630
We're counting on you.

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:32.170
<i>Sound Ship</i>'s today.

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:33.530
Nanase-san.

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:35.850
I'm not trying to put pressure on you, but...

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:38.680
Please do your best.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.560
That's sounds a lot like pressure to me...

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:45.610
We wanna brag about how amazing you are.

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:47.020
Right, Iori?

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:49.520
Well, you are our center.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:53.520
Relax.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.120
It's okay if you make mistakes.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:57.330
Forget the cameras are rolling.

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.120
Let's have fun in front of the audience.

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:03.160
We'll surprise the fans who 
have come to see other artists.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.500
Yeah!

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.120
Who's the most popular artist today?

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:08.920
TRIGGER, of course.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:12.920
I bet there will be a lot of
 TRIGGER fans again today.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:14.920
Hey.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:23.590
Good morning.

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:24.850
Looking forward to today.

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:27.850
Yeah. So are we.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.350
Tenn-nii, I...

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:37.700
Why are you standing right in the middle?

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:38.860
Huh?

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:41.910
Isn't it so you can lead 
them to greater heights?

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:46.030
You'd better do your best today, center.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.970
TRIGGER is impressive as always.

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.830
They have the auras of top idols.

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:53.730
Aura...

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:55.580
You've got one too, Rikkun.

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:56.010
Huh?

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:57.790
A healing aura.

00:01:57.790 --> 00:02:00.390
Can't that be your weapon?

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:02.140
Tamaki.

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:05.470
Everyone has their own kind of weapon.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:17.150
Gazing at the distant sky...

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:20.700
Someday we'll make it past there

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:26.180
Build a rainbow Next Harmony!

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:33.130
We don't know what's right

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:36.340
So we Try and Jump!

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:39.510
Slamming face first into 
challenges and laughing

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:43.140
For us It's Only Way!

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:46.320
Make it shake (For Your Sky)

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:49.820
Make it reach (For Your Heart)

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:52.310
We'll change any and all kinds of pain

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:53.470
Do Live! (Yeah!)

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:54.320
Live! (Yeah!)

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:57.740
In the light!

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.530
(One, Two, Three, Four, Five, Six, Seven Go!)

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:04.990
Yes Glory Days! Together 
we'll run through them

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:07.810
If your voice (Fuu!) reverberates (Dream!)

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:11.290
Then your wishes will become 
destiny (Singing New World!)

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:17.800
Give rise now to Age of Stage!

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:24.760
The future surely lies on the other side

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:27.680
Yes... It will keep on evolving

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:31.060
Our WiSH VOYAGE

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:37.320
Build a rainbow Next Harmony!

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:45.990
That Song Once Again

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:49.410
"Why are you standing right in the middle?

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.870
Isn't it so you can lead 
them to greater heights?"

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:53.620
Shut up!

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:59.210
You must really believe 
in our center to say that.

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:00.710
Of course.

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:05.650
How can he say that with a straight
 face? Isn't that embarrassing?

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:07.710
You're blushing.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.500
I am not!

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:12.370
Boys, get ready to leave.

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:14.140
We're canceling our performance.

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:16.250
Canceling?

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:19.650
We're entering the second 
half of <i>Sound Ship</i>.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:23.070
There's plenty more special performances 
from major artists coming up.

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:29.120
Thank you!

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:30.660
Good work.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.290
Yamato-san just spoke to me!

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:35.980
They're all TRIGGER fans.

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:39.490
A lot of TRIGGER fans don't like us.

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:41.300
Why? How could that be?

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:44.460
We were previously accused of 
trying to steal their fans.

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:46.380
It was our fault, though.

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:51.670
Yeah, but I doubt they'll all give 
the thumbs down when we perform.

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:53.640
I'm scared they'll start booing.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:55.820
What's wrong, Riku?

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:58.770
Nothing. I just noticed TRIGGER isn't coming.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:00.900
Probably in their room 
until the last minute.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.690
Oh, right.

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:07.820
Boys, it's nearly time.

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:08.650
Shall we go?

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:09.860
Yeah!

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:12.990
Canceled? But our fans are already here.

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:14.500
We can't leave now.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.880
Our president got into a fight
with the station higher-ups.

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:19.270
He said he wouldn't let TRIGGER perform.

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:20.460
What does that mean?

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:21.930
It's a grown-up thing.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:22.950
You must understand.

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:24.470
I can't accept this.

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:27.200
Our fans are here to see us.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:30.140
We can't disappoint them because 
of our own circumstances.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:31.900
Don't be so naive.

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:34.570
You're products of the agency.

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:36.990
You're used in deals and as secret weapons.

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:40.190
If you have a problem with 
that, go sing on the street.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:45.630
I'm saying if it's a "grown-up thing," 
they should settle it like grown-ups.

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:47.790
Excuse me!

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:51.020
I'm sorry. I heard there was 
a problem with the higher-ups.

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:53.080
We're on our way out right now.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:55.310
I'll do what I can to convince them.

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:57.280
Please wait here until you're on.

00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:58.320
I'm sorry.

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:00.290
You're wasting your time.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.320
We'll wait.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:02.430
Gaku!

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.030
Sorry, but we're counting on you.

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:08.160
Thank you.

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:12.010
What do you think you're doing?

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:14.650
What do <i>you</i> think <i>you're</i> doing?

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:15.910
I'm calling my dad.

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:16.560
Wa—

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:19.480
There's no convincing Gaku now.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:21.650
Naturally, we feel the same way.

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:24.140
Do what you like.

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:29.660
It's time for the next artist.

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:33.280
Overcoming waves of difficulty, 
they've finally made it aboard.

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:36.350
An idol group brimming with 
potential, they're IDOLiSH7.

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:38.410
They'll be singing "GOOD NIGHT AWESOME."

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:01.650
Cold rain the color of betrayal,

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:05.740
Runs down my cheek

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:11.160
I just know, these worn down emotions are

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:14.660
Gradation of fallen drops,

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:19.040
Passion begins to take control,

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:24.710
You just know, things will 
never be the way they were

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:25.250
(GOOD NIGHT AWESOME)

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:27.370
I7 is pretty good.

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:27.580
Believe in my fear...

00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:29.130
The guy with glasses is cool.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:30.960
Because these lost memories

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:32.470
Hey, that's the Clara Lowell model guy!

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:36.220
Loop obnoxiously often

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:42.240
What I want? I take it

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:39.800
Th-They're getting a lot of support.

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:41.870
I'm so moved. Of course they are.

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:43.100
They're all so handsome.

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:46.360
Ready go! Dark, Dark, Dark into the darkness

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:47.630
Don't be ridiculous!

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:49.580
I don't care about your circumstances!

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:52.400
The fans in the audience are here to see us!

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:53.820
<i>It's their mistake.</i>

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:56.030
<i>They're responsible for 
refunding the audience.</i>

00:07:56.030 --> 00:08:00.070
There you go again! Stop talking about money!

00:08:00.070 --> 00:08:03.370
We want to sing in front 
of that audience tonight!

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:05.240
<i>You just try it.</i>

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:09.130
<i>I have no problem destroying you 
so badly you'll never work again.</i>

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:12.100
<i>Your mother will be disappointed.</i>

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:16.090
<i>Your fans aren't the ones 
who allow you to sing.</i>

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:17.560
<i>It's because of me.</i>

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:18.800
<i>Don't get the wrong idea.</i>

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:19.780
Wait!

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:20.640
Damn it!

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:22.560
Satisfied?

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:26.330
That's too bad.

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:28.270
I wanted to see them from up close.

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:30.850
This is the opposite of the <i>Music Festa</i>.

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:34.700
We're the ones who aren't doing our job.

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:39.540
Where's our apology?

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:41.330
I'm sorry.

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:43.660
We're busy with the performance.

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:45.760
Are you ignoring TRIGGER?

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:49.460
What other artist could close the show?

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:51.650
Keep acting self-important.

00:08:51.650 --> 00:08:54.640
Someday our fans will abandon us, too.

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:58.640
Is there any way you'll perform?

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:00.310
No. No!

00:09:01.230 --> 00:09:03.230
Anesagi-san, please.

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:06.760
We are IDOLiSH7!

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:08.780
Thank you!

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:14.110
That was fun!

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:16.110
Water!

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:22.740
Nanase-san, you did well today.

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:23.870
Really?

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:25.500
I...

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:28.270
Yeah. The fans were into it, too.

00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:30.500
It didn't even feel like they 
were all TRIGGER fans.

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:32.700
I hope so.

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:37.720
More than half of the audience 
wasn't interested in us.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:41.180
But I wanted all of them to have 
fun, so I gave everything I had.

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:42.560
I...

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:45.290
That feeling reached them.

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:49.230
I'm sure it reached us and 
everyone watching on TV.

00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:52.980
I wish Tenn-nii had seen it.

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:55.610
I...

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:59.050
Yama-san, that sexy look you have in 
your eyes when you sing is pretty good.

00:09:59.050 --> 00:10:01.250
Well said, Tama!

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:05.040
Come in.

00:10:05.690 --> 00:10:07.140
Excuse me.

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:09.790
I'm sorry, but do you have a minute?

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:13.400
TRIGGER isn't performing?!

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:16.070
Our higher-ups got into an 
argument with their agency.

00:10:16.070 --> 00:10:17.970
They're refusing to perform.

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:21.010
Wait, right before they're on?

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:23.230
We're not sure what to do.

00:10:23.770 --> 00:10:28.270
We're asking other artists 
if they can close the show.

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:31.120
But no one wants to do it.

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:34.040
Most of the audience 
members are TRIGGER fans.

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:35.610
You could see their disappointment.

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:39.580
Is there any way you could do it?

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:46.050
I'm sorry, but we can't 
risk hurting our talent.

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:47.020
Let's do it.

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:47.830
Huh?

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:49.150
Are you guys okay with that?

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:52.000
Yeah. We should help each 
other out when we're in need.

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:55.960
And we already experienced a disappointed 
audience at the <i>Music Festa</i>.

00:10:55.960 --> 00:10:58.850
This isn't like that day, though.

00:10:58.850 --> 00:11:00.780
If we're not careful, they might even boo us.

00:11:00.780 --> 00:11:01.850
It's all right.

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:06.260
Thanks to you, we've grown up strong.

00:11:06.610 --> 00:11:11.930
Exactly. Let's deliver a dream-like experience
 to the fans who have supported us.

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:14.770
Manager, believe in us.

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:15.980
Guys...

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:18.900
Got it.

00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:20.810
Please get ready.

00:11:20.810 --> 00:11:22.130
Thank you.

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:30.490
It seems to be taking some time to prep
 the stage for the final performance.

00:11:30.490 --> 00:11:33.330
We're terribly sorry, but please
 hang in there a little longer.

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.300
TRIGGER's the final performance, right?

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:37.590
Maybe it's a really amazing performance.

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:39.510
Hurry up, TRIGGER!

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:40.510
TRIGGER!

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:44.400
TRIGGER! TRIGGER!

00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:52.590
TRIGGER! TRIGGER!

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:51.210
Thank you for waiting.

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:54.350
You've stuck with <i>Sound Ship</i> for a while now.

00:11:54.350 --> 00:11:57.970
<b>Tenn-kun! </b>

00:11:54.350 --> 00:11:57.980
The artist wrapping up our 
sea voyage is finally ready.

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:05.740
Once again, here is IDOLiSH7.

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:10.250
Good evening again!

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:11.600
Huh? I7?

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:12.370
Why?

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:16.690
Something came up, and TRIGGER 
is no longer able to perform.

00:12:16.690 --> 00:12:18.900
What?!

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:20.800
So we're performing in—

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:21.730
No!

00:12:21.730 --> 00:12:23.440
Put TRIGGER on!

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:25.140
TRIGGER!

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:26.760
...in their place!

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:32.420
TRIGGER! TRIGGER! TRIGGER!

00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:38.050
TRIGGER! TRIGGER! TRIGGER!

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:37.260
<b>Yamato 
</b>

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:37.260
<b>Notice me</b>

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:37.260
<b>Riku</b>

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:42.030
TRIGGER! TRIGGER!

00:12:40.770 --> 00:12:42.030
Shut up!

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:45.520
<b>Tenn-kun! </b>

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:46.780
Tamaki-kun?

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:51.090
We didn't plan to sing, either!

00:12:51.090 --> 00:12:53.200
We wanted to see them perform!

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:54.830
They're good role models.

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:58.880
If they can't come, none of us
 can do anything about it.

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:04.260
As long as we're here, let's sing 
TRIGGER's song together and go home.

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:05.600
But...

00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:07.260
That's not what we want.

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:10.570
TRIGGER fans, we're really...

00:13:10.570 --> 00:13:12.520
We're really, really sorry.

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:15.660
We're still nothing compared to them,

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:19.540
but we'll be singing TRIGGER's 
"NATSU shiyouze!"

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:22.300
NATSU Shiyouze!

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:23.650
Breaking Breaking Breaking 
Naked! (Let's dance!)

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:26.780
Shaking Shaking Shaking 
Your Heart! (Right now)

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:29.910
Making Making taboo (Love me?)

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:31.880
Taking Taking Taking!

00:13:31.880 --> 00:13:35.150
Let's do SUMMER!

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:37.930
(Oi! Oi!) Let's do SUMMER!

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:37.280
<b>Yamato 
</b>

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:37.280
<b>Riku</b>

00:13:36.770 --> 00:13:41.630
(Oi! Oi!) It's gotta be My way!

00:13:39.870 --> 00:13:44.380
(Oi! Oi!) Let's do SUMMER!

00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:45.680
(Oi! Oi!) How exciting!

00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:49.120
The burning sun and sky

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:52.040
<b>I love 
Ryunosuke!!</b>

00:13:46.910 --> 00:13:48.930
TRIGGER!

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:50.750
TRIGGER!

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:52.370
Light a fire in my curiosity

00:13:50.750 --> 00:13:53.840
TRIGGER! TRIGGER!

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:55.490
(So!) Mermaids at the water's edge

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:59.060
TRIGGER! TRIGGER! TRIGGER!

00:13:55.490 --> 00:13:59.060
(Bang!!) This High! feeling is absolute

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:19.660
TRIGGER! TRIGGER! TRIGGER!

00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:10.570
We can hear them all the way from here.

00:14:11.020 --> 00:14:14.000
They must've announced 
that we're not performing.

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:16.110
Ryu, put the TV on.

00:14:16.110 --> 00:14:17.230
You sure?

00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:20.090
I don't want to see the 
sad faces of our fans.

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:22.560
But we hurt them.

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:24.620
We have to accept it.

00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:30.900
<i>The burning sun and sky</i>

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:29.010
This is...

00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:34.200
<i>Light a fire in my curiosity</i>

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:35.420
IDOLiSH7.

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:37.250
<i>(So!) Mermaids at the water's edge</i>

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:37.640
Are they singing our song?

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:40.520
(Bang!!) This High! feeling is absolute

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:46.900
TRIGGER! TRIGGER! TRIGGER!

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:42.040
This is the only time of year

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:43.620
I've had enough! I feel so bad for I7!

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:43.900
Because this is the only time in our life

00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:45.120
Why'd they make them do this?!

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:46.900
Let's do it all with room to spare (Yeah!)

00:14:45.120 --> 00:14:46.900
Listen to them!

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:52.630
I'm sorry for forcing this role onto you.

00:14:52.630 --> 00:14:54.180
It's fine.

00:14:54.180 --> 00:14:54.930
Huh?

00:14:54.930 --> 00:14:57.740
Our idols can sing at full power,

00:14:57.740 --> 00:15:00.290
even if it's to an empty 
venue or while soaking wet.

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:05.170
I know their feelings, and their 
voices will reach the audience.

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:07.670
(So!) Mermaids at the water's edge

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:21.810
TRIGGER! TRIGGER! TRIGGER!

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:10.950
(Bang!!) This High! feeling is absolute

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:12.880
He's actually singing it well.

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:12.530
This is the only time of year

00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:14.120
Because this is the only time in our life

00:15:12.880 --> 00:15:14.800
Even though it's a TRIGGER song.

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:17.490
We have to do what we want 
and forget our troubles

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:17.060
They said they're their role models...

00:15:17.490 --> 00:15:20.880
Let's go driving, surfing, and 
even experience summer love

00:15:19.930 --> 00:15:21.810
They look like they're having fun.

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:24.150
Let's do it all with room to spare (Yeah!)

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:26.060
<i>I always wanted to become 
perfect, like Tenn-nii.</i>

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:27.460
The dangerous and loco girls'

00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:28.700
<i>I never came close, though.</i>

00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:30.490
Gazes made my heart pound

00:15:28.700 --> 00:15:31.360
<i>But there are things even I can do.</i>

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:36.830
It feels like something is starting and 
my chest is burning with anticipation

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:32.320
Let's go!

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:34.050
I guess this will do.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:38.310
Everyone's been talking 
about those Three Guys!

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:39.020
<i>This is what makes Nanase-san amazing.</i>

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:39.580
It might be us they're talking about!

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:41.440
If you'll give us a wonderful feeling

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:43.500
<i>Anyone else would've hated the idea.</i>

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:43.140
The answer is yes (Alright!)

00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:49.460
I'll hold you tight and welcome 
this invincible Sunshine

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:46.590
<i>Riku has no malice.</i>

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:48.910
<i>He's hardworking and honest.</i>

00:15:48.910 --> 00:15:51.090
<i>It makes you want to support him.</i>

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:55.890
Don't you feel like the 
impossible is Nothing Nothing?

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:54.090
<i>Dancing with him is so fun.</i>

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:56.230
Clap your hands! Come on!

00:15:55.890 --> 00:16:02.460
If we have as much fun as we can 
we might be fantastically Lucky

00:15:56.230 --> 00:15:57.100
Yeah!

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:09.150
This entire season is a 
thoroughly thrilling Good Night

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:07.860
Yeah!

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:10.740
Nice! Get yourselves pumped up!

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:15.330
We're the ones who will win, 
that sounds crazy good! (Wao!)

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:12.990
So TRIGGER can hear you!

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:17.370
Yes! Pump your love up even higher, hotter!

00:16:15.330 --> 00:16:19.370
(Oi! Oi!) Let's do SUMMER!

00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:23.370
(Oi! Oi!) It's gotta be My way!

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:26.320
<i>(Oi! Oi!) Let's do SUMMER!</i>

00:16:24.910 --> 00:16:27.810
<i>(Oi! Oi!) How exciting!</i>

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:34.880
They're singing our song with 
the fans who waited for us.

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:38.130
<b>I love </b>TRIGGER

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:38.140
<b>Tenn-kun! </b>

00:16:39.630 --> 00:16:41.020
This is rough.

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:43.470
It's hard to watch this.

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:48.920
<i>We're the ones who will win, 
that sounds crazy good! (Wao!)</i>

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:48.620
I've never felt so pathetic in my life.

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:53.700
<i>(Oi! Oi!) Let's do SUMMER!</i>

00:16:49.050 --> 00:16:53.690
They're doing what we couldn't, 
and they're doing it perfectly.

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:56.700
<i>(Oi! Oi!) It's gotta be My way!</i>

00:16:53.690 --> 00:16:56.720
Why aren't we standing up there?!

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:59.730
<i>(Oi! Oi!) Let's do SUMMER!</i>

00:16:57.230 --> 00:16:58.120
Damn it!

00:16:58.520 --> 00:17:01.120
<i>(Oi! Oi!) How exciting!</i>

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:01.930
Wow!

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:03.340
With us now! Ready, and...

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:06.140
(Oi! Oi!) Let's do SUMMER!

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:09.680
(Oi! Oi!) It's gotta be My way!

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:12.570
(Oi! Oi!) Let's do SUMMER!

00:17:09.230 --> 00:17:13.180
You've grown stronger, Riku.

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:13.880
<i>(Oi! Oi!) How exciting!</i>

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:17.580
We're gonna run through!!

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:31.740
IDOLiSH7! They sang TRIGGER's song!

00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:33.890
Bring me a new song immediately!

00:17:33.890 --> 00:17:36.990
We can't let TRIGGER sing a tainted song!

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:39.930
I-In that case, we can 
use one of my old songs.

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:43.120
If TRIGGER sings the song 
that gave me my big break—

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:45.210
Your old songs are worthless!

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:48.570
The only thing that has value is 
your reputation for writing hits!

00:17:48.570 --> 00:17:50.960
Though that should be stripped from you soon.

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:55.350
Your most recent new song was well-received.

00:17:55.350 --> 00:17:58.680
I expect you to bring me something in 
the same style, but even higher quality.

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:00.470
The same style?

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:02.590
Don't try and claim you can't.

00:18:02.590 --> 00:18:06.220
If you don't bring it to me in three 
days, I'm cutting ties with you.

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:09.030
What is it?

00:18:09.030 --> 00:18:12.850
<i>The higher-ups of the TV station would like 
to apologize for the </i>Sound Ship<i> incident.</i>

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:15.810
They should've apologized sooner.

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:18.570
The same style...

00:18:25.050 --> 00:18:26.320
Damn it!

00:18:26.320 --> 00:18:27.210
Where are they?

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:28.710
They must have more!

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:30.460
Damn!

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:31.840
You can't be serious!

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:33.890
No one even knows who they are.

00:18:33.890 --> 00:18:35.740
They have no idea how hard I've worked.

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:39.720
Excuse us.

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:51.880
<b>King Pudding</b>

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:47.100
Nobody's even gonna be here this late.

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:48.620
I still want to say it, just in case.

00:18:48.620 --> 00:18:50.990
Come on. Go get the things you forgot.

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:51.900
Okay.

00:18:52.810 --> 00:18:54.150
Wait.

00:18:54.850 --> 00:18:55.960
Someone's here.

00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:57.160
Who?

00:18:57.160 --> 00:18:58.640
Another burglar?

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:05.490
Who's there?!

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:08.830
Watch out!

00:19:08.240 --> 00:19:09.310
Tamaki-kun!

00:19:20.730 --> 00:19:22.330
Okay. Okay.

00:19:22.330 --> 00:19:24.550
So you're not hurt or anything?

00:19:24.550 --> 00:19:27.230
He just whacked me
 a little with a flashlight.

00:19:27.230 --> 00:19:28.810
So-chan made it sound worse than it is.

00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:30.810
Sorry...

00:19:30.810 --> 00:19:32.240
We were so scared.

00:19:32.240 --> 00:19:35.850
Sogo was suddenly yelling for 
an ambulance and bandages.

00:19:35.850 --> 00:19:38.110
He actually scared <i>me</i>.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:40.730
How dare you hit Tamaki-kun...

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:46.120
So-chan, wait! Wait!

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:48.140
You'll kill him! You're gonna kill him!

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:51.040
I was worried something had happened to you.

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:52.530
I was confused.

00:19:52.530 --> 00:19:55.440
Can't you be confused less violently?

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:58.250
We're fine. Could you take 
care of things there?

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:00.510
Got it. Take care.

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:03.760
What are we going to do with him?

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:05.740
It seems his agency didn't tell him do it.

00:20:05.740 --> 00:20:08.050
He acted on his own.

00:20:08.050 --> 00:20:10.560
N-Not the police...

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:13.730
We've decided not to file a police report.

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:17.840
If this story got out, it 
could hurt TRIGGER, too.

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:20.320
That would be hard for their fans.

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:24.290
The president said he'd 
go talk to them himself.

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:25.950
Will he be all right?

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:29.870
The facts are exactly as I've described them.

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:32.080
We don't plan on making an issue out of this.

00:20:33.230 --> 00:20:36.210
Did you come all the way 
here to get your song back?

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:40.380
No. I just wanted to tell you something.

00:20:42.160 --> 00:20:45.040
You rose in this industry 
based on your talents.

00:20:45.450 --> 00:20:49.060
My agency can't compare to how 
massive your production company is.

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:51.770
But haven't you forgotten 
something important?

00:20:52.080 --> 00:20:53.640
What are you talking about?

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:56.780
This job is about making people happy.

00:20:56.780 --> 00:21:00.150
Your clients, your fans, and 
the people you work with.

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:05.410
If you don't take good care of people, 
someday you'll make a huge mistake.

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:09.820
How ridiculous. People are 
meant to be controlled.

00:21:10.270 --> 00:21:14.790
I made it this far by controlling my 
clients, fans, and business partners.

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:18.290
My success proves that I was right.

00:21:18.860 --> 00:21:21.670
Take good care of people? 
Don't make me laugh.

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:24.670
You drove your own wife to an early grave!

00:21:24.670 --> 00:21:29.150
Musubi lived a full life 
and left me a treasure.

00:21:29.150 --> 00:21:30.890
My beloved daughter.

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:33.100
I could've made her happier!

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:37.020
You have a fine son of your own.

00:21:37.490 --> 00:21:40.700
I'd take care not to trouble him
 by making more enemies.

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:44.050
Wait, Takanashi!

00:21:44.960 --> 00:21:46.370
Oh, excuse me.

00:21:46.370 --> 00:21:47.920
Ah, no problem.

00:21:53.100 --> 00:21:56.000
Now I owe Takanashi a favor.

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:57.970
That idiot composer.

00:21:57.970 --> 00:22:00.590
Wasn't that the president 
of Takanashi Productions?

00:22:00.590 --> 00:22:02.050
What are you doing here?

00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:04.080
It's about <i>Sound Ship</i>.

00:22:04.080 --> 00:22:06.550
I demand an explana—

00:22:06.550 --> 00:22:07.710
Shut up!

00:22:07.710 --> 00:22:09.920
I have nothing to say to you!

00:22:09.920 --> 00:22:11.220
Get out!

00:22:11.220 --> 00:22:13.390
Oh, really?

00:22:16.160 --> 00:22:18.490
I'll crush them completely.

00:22:18.490 --> 00:22:21.270
Both Takanashi Productions and his daughter.

00:22:22.110 --> 00:22:24.240
And IDOLiSH7!

00:22:34.410 --> 00:22:37.740
Start running (beyond)

00:22:37.740 --> 00:22:44.960
Your imagination... Alive

00:22:53.100 --> 00:22:58.610
If you desire something from 
the bottom of your heart

00:22:58.610 --> 00:23:03.310
Risk your life and dive in

00:23:03.310 --> 00:23:08.400
The resolve to discard what's truly important

00:23:08.400 --> 00:23:13.530
Is the boat that will take you to new sights

00:23:13.530 --> 00:23:16.080
(Hey man!) Take the strings of your heart

00:23:16.390 --> 00:23:18.620
(Hey man!) And stretch them

00:23:18.620 --> 00:23:21.500
(Say dream!) To the limit

00:23:21.500 --> 00:23:26.800
At the other end you're sure 
to find the Gate to paradise

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:32.450
You'll be the first witness

00:23:32.450 --> 00:23:37.240
Our pounding pulses are Heavenly

00:23:37.240 --> 00:23:42.230
Admit that you can't deny it

00:23:42.230 --> 00:23:46.690
We start... What do your fingertips

00:23:46.690 --> 00:23:51.260
Seek now?
